        "original_id": "10d50d8c-e6a3-59f1-a54b-a02afe247e6e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Istanbul, Turkey, Golden Horn, Vefa\n- Structures: Kalenderhane Mosque, Galata Bridge, Aqueduct of Valens, Vefa Kilise, Süleymaniye Mosque\n- Concepts: Eastern Orthodox church, mosque, Byzantine monuments, Ottoman monuments\n\nFacts:\n- Kalenderhane Mosque in Istanbul was formerly an Eastern Orthodox church and was converted into a mosque by the Ottomans.\n- Galata Bridge is a bridge in Istanbul, Turkey, that spans the Golden Horn.\n- Vefa lies roughly northwest of the eastern section of the Aqueduct of Valens.\n- Vefa has many monuments, including the Byzantine-related Kalenderhane Mosque and Vefa Kilise.\n- Vefa also has Ottoman monuments, including the Süleymaniye Mosque.",
